# Code style

## Logging

- Use the shared `logger` from `src/utils/logger.ts` (default export) for all runtime diagnostics.
- Never use `console.log`, `console.error`, `console.warn`, `console.info`, or `console.debug` anywhere under `src/`.
- Reasoning: the project pipes `logger` output to a rotating log file (`tslog.log`) and applies consistent pretty-print styles. `console.*` bypasses both, so messages are lost on rotation and look out of place alongside the rest of the log stream.

Import as:

```ts
import logger from '<path-to>/utils/logger';
// ...
logger.error('Something went wrong:', error);
```
